Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 11:37:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sound): reconcile block interaction and placement audio

Java 26.3 plays door, trapdoor, fence gate, and button sounds when the local player interacts. Bedrock then echoes a matching level sound event, so forwarding it makes the player hear two sounds. Track the local click briefly and consume only the matching event at that block, leaving redstone and other players audible.

Record local block placement and consume only matching Bedrock echoes, including placement at replaceable blocks. Forward unrelated placement sounds from other players and retain door audio across connections.
